      "{FileName: KnightLaw_FAQs.md}\n{H1: Frequently Asked Questions (Initial Intake Call)}\n# Frequently Asked Questions (Initial Intake Call)\n### Where are you located?\n\n**A:** We have four offices strategically located across California, allowing us to serve clients throughout the state.\n### What do we do?\n\n**A:** We help consumers get out of their defective vehicles and get back the money paid in regard to their sales contract/lease agreement. The California Lemon Law makes it favorable to the consumer because it requires the car manufacturer to replace or repurchase your vehicle when they fail to conform it to warranty after a reasonable number of repair attempts.",
      "{FileName: knight-law-group-faqs-14-07-2026.md}\nTherefore, we are unable to assist you.\n---\n24. **Do you help consumers who have used vehicles?**\nOnly if the vehicle was sold used CPO (Certified pre-owned) or used – dealer demo.\nIf it was used without being CPO or a dealer demo, no, unfortunately we cannot help.\n---\n25. **What is a buyback?\nWhat is it that you are recovering for me?**\nA buyback under California's Lemon Law is when the manufacturer repurchases your defective vehicle.\nWe seek to recover the payments you made toward the purchase or lease of the vehicle, including finance charges paid, sales or use tax, license and initial registration fees, and other official acquisition fees required under your purchase or lease agreement—less the legally required mileage offset for the use of the vehicle before the defect first occurred.\n---\n26. **What do I need to do during my case?\nWhat is my participation?**\nClient participation is limited but required throughout the process.\nYou must keep us updated if your contact information changes, provide any documents or information we request, and continue taking your vehicle to the dealership for repairs if problems persist, sending us the repair records from each visit.\nDepending on your case you may also be asked to:\n* Answer written questions (interrogatories) about your ownership experience.\n* Allow a vehicle inspection.\nWe'll schedule a convenient time, pick up your vehicle, take it to the inspection, and return it the same day.\nYou do not need to be present.\n* Participate in a deposition, where you'll answer questions under oath about your ownership experience.\nDepositions take place outside of court, and our attorneys will fully prepare you beforehand, either in person or by phone.\n* Attend a court hearing or trial, if necessary.\nIn some cases, you may be required to participate in a Mandatory Settlement Conference (MSC) or a trial.\nIf that happens, our attorneys will prepare you in advance, explain what to expect, and be with you throughout the process.\n---",
      "{FileName: KnightLaw_FAQs.md}\n{H1: Frequently Asked Questions (Initial Intake Call)}\n### What is a repurchase/buyback?\n\n**A:** A repurchase/buyback is the amount the manufacturer is required to refund you. This includes the down payment, monthly payments, interest paid, and taxes found on the face of your sales contract/lease agreement.\n### What is a reasonable number of attempts?\n\n**A:** To be able to assist you, we need to see a history of visits/presentations to the dealership. The California Lemon Law does not specify a number; it only describes a “reasonable” amount. If you’ve had previous visits, we would like to review your repair orders."
    ],
